.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-15.verdict.txt:24:3. Context-pressure code: context_pressure.py is the same text, including the symlink protections (O_EXCL, O_NOFOLLOW, a random tmp name, mode 0600) and the fail-open re-arm. Every free name it reads is in some part's __all__. I checked the compaction.py exports: _GC_MARKER_WALL_BUDGET_S, _CONTEXT_PRESSURE_STATE_BASENAME and the SID/TTL/GC constants. So the GC path cannot raise a NameError that its (OSError, TypeError, ValueError) guard would miss.
.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/codex-rc1-04.verdict.txt:5:The default-enabled shadow gate persists state using a predictable temporary pathname opened with O_TRUNC. A pre-existing symlink there redirects truncation and JSON writes into another adopter file; a symlinked parent also redirects storage. The subsequent replace does not undo that damage. Minimal fix: reject symlinked parents, create a unique temporary file exclusively inside a verified directory, and replace through that directory; skip persistence when storage is unsafe. Confirmed by source tracing, without exercising destructive writes.
.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-23.verdict.txt:59:   - Problem: `--include-plans` uses `cp -pR`, which keeps symlinks found under .claude/plans, while the restore validator refuses any link member.
.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-27.verdict.txt:17:Failure scenario: ceo-backup.sh --include-plans still copies plans with `cp -pR`, which keeps symlinks as symlinks (GNU and BSD cp). tar then stores them as SYMTYPE members, and the backup exits 0 with a valid sha256 sidecar. Before staging anything, ceo-restore.sh runs `_restore_archive.py <tarball>`, which refuses any non-file, non-dir member ("refused member type"), and exits 2. The whole archive is refused, including audit/ and memory/, even without --restore-plans. Pre-1.4.4 backups whose memory/ held a link fail the same way. So the framework's own backup can produce an archive that its documented restore command (DISASTER-RECOVERY.md Scenarios B/D) refuses, and this shows up only during a disaster. Manual `tar -x` still works.
.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-27.verdict.txt:30:VERDICT: GO-WITH-CONDITIONS Every declared condition this payload touches (3b, 3c, 7) holds and there is no P0, but one new P1 goes to the annex: ceo-backup.sh --include-plans keeps symlinks, so ceo-restore.sh refuses the whole archive; it should be carried as declared-open or fixed before GA.
.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/codex-rc1-27.verdict.txt:12:Remaining preflight gap: ancestors are checked for symlinks but not for non-directory files. If DEST/memory is a regular file, preview succeeds; apply can overwrite audit files before mkdir fails. Partial application was already possible before this delta. Minimal fix: validate every existing ancestor and required directory before any destination writes.
.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/codex-rc1-29.verdict.txt:9:In a core.symlinks=false checkout, Git records mode 120000 but materializes the link payload as a regular file. The new term scanner unconditionally calls readlink(), which raises EINVAL and makes the gate exit 2 even for clean content. Minimal fix: support both representations through the no-follow reader, preserving refusal of missing indexed links.

